DynamicPopups - Read MeThis example demonstrates how to implement a dynamic popup menu (a menu with different menu items per instance). One of the menu items also tests how to show and hide the menu bar.The basic mechanism is to programmatically add menu items to an otherwise empty CMNU.  Althoughnot shown in this example, there are functions for adding and removing menu items with CommandNumbers associated with them.  This example demonstrates how to add menu items without CommandNumbers, varyingthe label for the last item (the document name).  It also demonstrates how to implement how to respondto a menu selection that doesn't have a CommandNumber associated with it, in this case, showing/hiding the menu bar.